<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44365" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sincĭput</span></b> ,
		pĭtis, n.
		semi - caput; cf.: sinciput <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμικεφάλιον,
				ἡμίκρανον, ἡμικέφαλον</span>, Gloss. Philox..
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Half a head;</i> of the smoked <i>cheek</i>, <i>jowl</i> of a hog, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Men.
				1, 3, 28</span></i> (Ritschl, sincipitamenta); <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 51,
				77, § 209</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pers. 6,
			70</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 13, 85</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>The brain</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non tibi Sanum est, adulescens, sinciput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Men. 3, 2, 41</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 2, 69</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>The head</i>, in gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miserabile sinciput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 5, 419</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
